<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani yarn rates end steady, seen stable.</title>
<headline>Pakistani yarn rates end steady, seen stable.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-03-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistani cotton yarn rates ended steady on Saturday and dealers said prices would remain stable, reflecting a calm domestic cotton market.</p>
<p>Rates in rupees supplied by the Pakistan Yarn Merchant Association for a 10-lb (4.54 kg) cone of 21 counts:</p>
<p>				     Saturday     Previous</p>
<p>    Al-Karam (A.K.)	    485	    485</p>
<p>    Shafiq (Gold ky.)	  450	    450</p>
<p>    Globe (Hina)		 480	    480</p>
<p>    ($1 = 40.22 rupees)    -- Amir Zia 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
